<article class="env-variant" id="058A">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/058A">Variant <span data-tag="058A">4.7.6.9</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a differential graded category. For every integer $n \geq -1$, the following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The differential graded nerve $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{dg}}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ is locally $n$-truncated. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For every pair of objects $X,Y \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the homology groups $\mathrm{H}_{m}( \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(X,Y)_{\ast } )$ vanish for $m &gt; n$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> See Example <a data-tag="06QW" href="/tag/06QW">4.7.1.9</a>. </p>
</article>
